DESCRIPTION:Geographic Information Systems Day\, usually just GIS Day\, is 
 the mapping world's open house: one day on which county GIS departments\, 
 universities and utilities show the public what they do with spatial data.
  Esri\, the software company that runs the day's website\, dates the first
  formal GIS Day to 1999 and credits the consumer advocate Ralph Nader with
  inspiring it. It falls on the third Wednesday of November\, inside Geogra
 phy Awareness Week\, which puts it on November 18 in 2026.\n\nhttps://toda
 ycelebrates.com/holiday/geographic-information-systems-day/
